Duplicate declarations warn while the first declaration remains authoritative.

========== CLI ==========

ledlight accounts --format json <<'LEDGER'
commodity SEK
  default
commodity FUND ; fund
  format 1,000.0000 FUND
commodity FUND ; duplicate
commodity UNUSED
commodity EUR
commodity NOK
tag Declared
tag Declared ; duplicate
tag Receipt
tag Reviewed
tag Source
account Assets:Fund ; primary
account Assets:Fund ; duplicate
account Assets:Unused
account Equity:Opening
P 2024-01-02 FUND 12.5 SEK ; closing
P 2024-01-01 EUR 11 NOK
P 2024-01-02 FUND 13 SEK ; corrected

2024-01-03 Tagged ; :Reviewed:
  ; Source: import.csv
  Assets:Fund  1 FUND {10 SEK} ; Receipt: 42
  Equity:Opening  -10 SEK
LEDGER

========== OUTPUT ==========

[
  "Assets:Fund",
  "Equity:Opening"
]

========== WARNINGS ==========

[MISSING_COMMODITY_FORMAT] Commodity SEK must declare a format property
  <stdin>:1:1

[DUPLICATE_COMMODITY_DECLARATION] Commodity FUND has already been declared
  <stdin>:5:1

[MISSING_COMMODITY_FORMAT] Commodity UNUSED must declare a format property
  <stdin>:6:1

[MISSING_COMMODITY_FORMAT] Commodity EUR must declare a format property
  <stdin>:7:1

[MISSING_COMMODITY_FORMAT] Commodity NOK must declare a format property
  <stdin>:8:1

[DUPLICATE_TAG_DECLARATION] Tag Declared has already been declared
  <stdin>:10:1

[DUPLICATE_ACCOUNT_DECLARATION] Account Assets:Fund has already been declared
  <stdin>:15:1
